sequenceDiagram
    actor Author
    participant Sign as polar-sign
    participant Front as Credentials front
    participant CredAgent as Credentials agent
    participant Repo as Repo and scheduler
    participant Config as Target config
    participant Crypto as Target crypto

    Note over Author,Front: The schema export marks secret fields, so the tool knows which to encrypt
    Author->>Sign: encrypt item.dhall for agent X
    Sign->>Front: public escrow key for agent X (mTLS, user certificate)
    Front->>CredAgent: AgentEscrowKeyRequest
    CredAgent-->>Front: public key only
    Front-->>Sign: public key of agent X
    Sign->>Sign: encrypt each secret field to that key, bound to agent, field and version
    Sign-->>Author: plaintext secret never written to the file

    Author->>Sign: sign item.dhall
    Sign-->>Author: signature covers the ciphertext
    Author->>Repo: push, then delivery as in the delivery diagram

    Repo-)Config: document for agent X
    Config->>Config: verify the signature and every other check first
    Config->>Crypto: DecryptOwnMessage for each secret field
    Crypto-->>Config: plaintext (private key stays in custody)
    Config->>Config: apply, plaintext is never recorded or reported

    Note over Config,CredAgent: Closing the loop, retried until acknowledged
    Config->>Crypto: escrow the secret to the credentials agent
    Crypto->>CredAgent: EscrowKeyRequest, then StoreSecret
    CredAgent-->>Crypto: stored
    Crypto-->>Config: loop closed

    Note over Config,CredAgent: Later, whenever the agent needs it
    Crypto->>CredAgent: RetrieveSecret
    CredAgent-->>Crypto: re-encrypted to the agent's own certificate
